{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-14-Oct-2022-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Find the average of all prime numbers between 10 and 20.", "options": [{"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A and B undertake a contract of a task for ₹7,500. A can do complete the task all alone in 50 days and B can complete the same task all by himself in 60 days. However, to finish the work early, they take C’s help and complete the entire work in 20 days. What is the difference (in ₹) between B’s and C’s share for their contribution in completing the task?", "options": [{"text": "250", "added": false}, {"text": "500", "added": false}, {"text": "2,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "wages", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The sum of two numbers is 15 and the difference between their squares is also 15. Which of the following is the larger number?", "options": [{"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The price of oil has increased by 35%. By what percentage should the increased price of oil be reduced so that the price of oil remains the same?", "options": [{"text": "33.33%", "added": false}, {"text": "25.93%", "added": false}, {"text": "27.92%", "added": false}, {"text": "35%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "Two trains 250 m and 300 m long are running on parallel rails in the same direction at speeds of 80 km/h and 65 km/h, respectively. Time taken by the faster train to cross the slower train will be:", "options": [{"text": "132 s", "added": false}, {"text": "232 s", "added": false}, {"text": "322 s", "added": false}, {"text": "130 s", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A cylindrical pillar has a curved surface area of 264 m2 and a volume of 924 m3. What is the ratio of the diameter and height?", "options": [{"text": "7 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2017", "added": false}, {"text": "2015", "added": false}, {"text": "2019", "added": false}, {"text": "2018", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "fractions-decimals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "centres-and-medians", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "160", "added": false}, {"text": "140", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "170", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-fractions", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "The value of a machine increased by 10% for two years and then depreciated by 8% in the third year. If the value of the machine three years ago was ₹2,50,000, then what is the value of the machine now?", "options": [{"text": "₹2,78,300", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,78,780", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,85,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,77,300", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "What is the difference between the largest and the smallest two digit prime numbers?", "options": [{"text": "86", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "91", "added": false}, {"text": "84", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "types-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "A takes twice as long as B and C together take to complete a work, and B takes twice as long as A and C together. However, A, B and C together can complete the work in 30 days. How long would C alone take to complete the work?", "options": [{"text": "50 days", "added": false}, {"text": "72 days", "added": false}, {"text": "63 days", "added": false}, {"text": "90 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "By selling an ornament for Rs.720, Chaitra loses 10%. At what price should she sell it in order to gain 15%?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.720.00", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.800.00", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.920.00", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.745.20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "√3", "added": false}, {"text": "3√3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The simple interest on Rs.7,300 at 15% p.a. from 28 April to 4 November, approximately is:", "options": [{"text": "Rs.750.00", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.570.00", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,095.00", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.547.50", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "A shopkeeper sold calculators at Rs.1,081 each after 6% discount on the labelled price. Had he not given the discount, he would have earned a profit of 15% on the cost price. What was the cost price of each calculator?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.985", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.975", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.945", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixed / Composite", "sub": "two-topic-composite", "key_answer": null}]}